opennyai_summary.decision:
Since the deceased was a bachelor, out of the total income, 50% is to be deducted towards personal expenses of the deceased.
Then the compensation towards loss of dependency would be Rs.10,58,400/- (Rs.4,900/- x 12 x 18).
Keeping in mind the judgment of Supreme Court, the revised compensation to which the appellants are entitled, would be as follows:
